# FBM salience-gate — drop compaction-summary context-dump episodes

Per `docs/plans/fbm-salience-gate-compaction-summary-dump.md`.
Single-component amendment on the EXISTING `framework/primary-persona/`
component; advances the existing sidecar.

The episode salience gate (`compute_salience`,
`framework/primary-persona/src/loam/primary_persona/file_memory.py`)
recognized only four structural junk shapes (task-notification,
channel/scaffolding-empty, empty-user, bare-ack). A compaction-summary
context-dump — a turn whose user half OPENS with "This session is being
continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context", followed
by a multi-thousand-word summary naming every active objective — matched
none of them, so it rode at full salience and BM25-dominated almost every
work-anchored query (it is long + carries every objective keyword). It was
the single worst recall polluter on the live episode store (19 such
episodes; diagnosis: loam-fbm-relevance-assessment §1.3).

This cycle adds the 5th junk signature inside the existing, tested gate —
same mechanism, same `SALIENCE_JUNK` return, same never-drop floor (the
episode stays on disk; only its retrieval salience drops). Deterministic,
no LLM, stdlib-only (`feedback_no_anthropic_api_key`).

  - AC-FBM-SAL-7 — `compute_salience` returns `SALIENCE_JUNK` for a user
    half opening with the compaction-summary continuation marker
    (`_COMPACTION_SUMMARY_MARKER`); the four prior signatures untouched.
  - AC-FBM-SAL-8 — a genuine Luke turn that merely MENTIONS a continuation
    in prose stays `SALIENCE_FULL` (no false positive; the signature keys
    on the dump's structural OPENING, not incidental token overlap —
    protect-real-messages, sibling of AC-FBM-SAL-5).
  - AC-FBM-SAL-9 (outcome-altitude) — a real `retrieve()` call through the
    production write -> search -> merge path, no pre-arranged retrieval
    state: the dump does NOT surface; a genuinely-relevant episode does.

Non-regression: AC-FBM-SAL-1..6 stay green (the four prior signatures
unchanged, substantive turns still surface, the never-delete floor holds,
the threshold stays re-tunable, the spread-neighbor gating holds).

No ODD violation in surrounding code; the fix adds one deterministic
signature, no defensive code for unnamed cases.
